GitHub Actions Workflow Syntax (YAML Basics)

Today I focused on understanding how GitHub Actions workflows are written using YAML, which is the backbone of CI/CD automation.

🔹 Workflow Structure
A workflow is defined in a YAML file inside: .github/workflows/
It contains:
Workflow name
Trigger events
Jobs to execute

🔹 Key YAML Keywords
name → Human-readable workflow name
on → Events that trigger workflow
jobs → Tasks executed by runners
These define what runs and when.

🔹 Indentation Rules
YAML is indentation-sensitive
Spaces are used (not tabs)
Wrong indentation = workflow failure
Proper structure is critical.

🔹 YAML Best Practices
Keep workflows readable
Use meaningful names
Avoid deep nesting
Comment complex steps

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
YAML defines automation.
 Structure controls execution.
 Clean syntax prevents failures.
